## Check the implementation

Test no initial answer, changed selection, persistence after an error, arrow keys and long labels. On small screens stack choices rather than squeezing several targets into one row.

Use the [civica accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS radios](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/radios) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica markup, Arial typography and civica assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

